TYPES OF MOBILE INTERNET NETWORKS

2G  Second Generation
    Speed: 100-300 kbps
    First mobile data (GSM/CDMA era)

3G  Third Generation
    Speed: 1-3 Mbps
    First mobile broadband (UMTS/HSPA)

4G  Fourth Generation
    Speed: 5-100 Mbps
    Faster + more reliable (LTE foundation)

4G LTE  Enhanced 4G
    Speed: 10-150 Mbps
    Improved latency and capacity over basic 4G

5G  Fifth Generation
    Speed: 1-10 Gbps
    Ultra-fast + very low latency (mmWave + sub-6)
